From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joonhoe Kim <26rote@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 15:03:25 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] ipa: softisp: Add a contrast detection autofocus

Add an Af algorithm to the software ISP IPA module. It uses the focus
statistics: a coarse scan through the lens range from the far end,
stopped once the contrast has clearly passed its peak, a fine scan
between the neighbours of the peak, and the interpolated maximum as the
result. A scan whose contrast varies by less than a quarter found
nothing to focus on and leaves the lens at the default position.

The lens moves right after a frame with statistics, so it has the three
frames in between to settle. In continuous mode the scan runs once the
exposure has settled after the start, and again when the contrast of the
focused scene has differed from its reference for four statistics frames
in a row.

Controls: AfMode (manual, auto, continuous), AfTrigger and LensPosition;
metadata: AfMode, AfState, LensPosition and FocusFoM. The mapping from
dioptres to lens driver positions is linear between two positions given
in the tuning data. The algorithm is inert when the camera has no lens.
